<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Password Strength Enhancement</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/app.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="site-header">
    <div class="inner">
        <a class="brand" href="/">Password Strength Enhancement</a>
        <span class="header-note">Prototype</span>
    </div>
</header>
<main class="shell" data-initial="<%= locals.tab || 'signup' %>">

    <section class="intro">
        <h1>Colour your password to make it harder to guess</h1>
        <p class="lead">Choose a password, then assign a colour to any of its characters. The server stores each character together with its colour, so the same letters in a different colour pattern are a different password.</p>

        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <div class="how">
            <div class="item"><h3>Choose a password</h3><p>Use at least six characters with upper case, lower case, a digit and one of @ $ ! % * ? &amp;.</p></div>
            <div class="item"><h3>Colour characters</h3><p>Select characters, then pick a colour from the palette. Characters you leave uncoloured count as having no colour.</p></div>
            <div class="item"><h3>Repeat it at login</h3><p>Enter the same password and apply the same colours. A correct password with the wrong colours is rejected.</p></div>
        </div>

        <div class="spec-wrap">
            <table class="spec">
                <caption>Estimated strength of <code>Abc12@x</code> (7 characters, 72-symbol pool)</caption>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><th scope="row">No colours</th><td>43 bits</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">3 characters coloured</th><td>53 bits</td></tr>
                    <tr><th scope="row">All 7 characters coloured</th><td>65 bits</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="spec-note">Estimate: log2 of the symbol pool for each character, plus log2(9) bits for each coloured character, because an attacker must also guess one of nine colours.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card" aria-label="Account">
        <% if (locals.error) { %>
            <div class="alert" role="alert"><%= error %></div>
        <% } %>

        <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
            <button class="tab" role="tab" type="button" data-tab="signup" aria-selected="true">Sign up</button>
            <button class="tab" role="tab" type="button" data-tab="login" aria-selected="false">Log in</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Sign up -->
        <div class="panel" data-panel="signup">
            <h2>Create an account</h2>
            <p class="sub">The colours you choose are part of your password. You need them to log in.</p>
            <form class="auth-form" data-mode="signup" method="post" action="/register" novalidate>
                <div class="field" data-field="username">
                    <label for="su-user">Username</label>
                    <input type="text" id="su-user" name="userName" placeholder="6-15 letters, numbers or _ @ # +" autocomplete="username" required>
                    <div class="hint-err">Username must be 6-15 characters (letters, numbers, _ @ # +).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="field" data-field="email">
                    <label for="su-email">Email</label>
                    <input type="email" id="su-email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" required>
                    <div class="hint-err">Enter a valid email address.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="field" data-field="password">
                    <label for="su-pw">Password</label>
                    <div class="pw-wrap">
                        <input type="password" id="su-pw" data-pw autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="Create a password">
                        <button type="button" class="link-btn" data-toggle>Show</button>
                    </div>
                    <input type="hidden" name="pswd" data-encoded>
                    <div class="hint-err">Use at least 6 characters with upper case, lower case, a digit and one of @ $ ! % * ? &amp;.</div>

                    <%- include('partials/colorbox') %>

                    <div class="meter">
                        <div class="meter-bar"><div class="meter-fill" data-meter-fill></div></div>
                        <div class="meter-row">
                            <span>Strength: <span class="meter-label" data-meter-label>—</span></span>
                            <span class="bonus" data-meter-bonus></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="rules">
                        <li data-rule="len">6+ characters</li>
                        <li data-rule="lower">Lower case</li>
                        <li data-rule="upper">Upper case</li>
                        <li data-rule="digit">A digit</li>
                        <li data-rule="special">@ $ ! % * ? &amp;</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <button type="submit" class="btn">Create account</button>
            </form>
        </div>

        <!-- Log in -->
        <div class="panel" data-panel="login" hidden>
            <h2>Log in</h2>
            <p class="sub">Enter your password and apply the same colours you chose when you signed up.</p>
            <form class="auth-form" data-mode="login" method="post" action="/login">
                <div class="field">
                    <label for="li-email">Email</label>
                    <input type="email" id="li-email" name="email" placeholder="you@example.com" autocomplete="email" required>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label for="li-pw">Password</label>
                    <div class="pw-wrap">
                        <input type="password" id="li-pw" data-pw autocomplete="current-password" placeholder="Your password" required>
                        <button type="button" class="link-btn" data-toggle>Show</button>
                    </div>
                    <input type="hidden" name="pswd" data-encoded>
                    <%- include('partials/colorbox') %>
                </div>
                <button type="submit" class="btn">Log in</button>
            </form>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>
<footer class="site-footer">Prototype. Do not use a password you use elsewhere.</footer>
<script src="/js/auth.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
